[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124174,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Arsenical keratoses present as multiple hyperkeratotic lesions with a predilection for the hands and feet, following chronic exposure to arsenic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124175,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8070/0 Arsenical keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124176,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EK90.Y &amp; XH5NG4 Other discrete epidermal dysplasias &amp; Arsenical keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124177,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124178,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124179,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although the anatomical distribution is broad, the hands and feet (particularly the palms and soles) are most commonly affected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124180,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with diffuse or localized hyperpigmentation and raindrop pigmentation affecting mainly the trunk, as well as yellowish hyperkeratotic papules and confluent verrucous plaques with a predilection for palmoplantar skin, measuring 2&ndash;10&nbsp;mm and developing with a latency of decades after arsenic exposure {8125698; 23370535; 9169318; 29387754}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124181,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The incidence in high-income countries is very low; the disease occurs predominantly in poorer nations, due to contamination of the groundwater {29387754}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124182,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The main reasons for chronic arsenic exposure include environmental, medicinal, and occupational exposure.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124183,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chronic arsenic exposure promotes oxidative stress, which leads to antioxidant depletion, immune dysfunction, genotoxicity, impaired DNA repair, and disrupted signal transduction {25173797}. A pathogenetic role of HPV has also been postulated {11028865}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124184,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124185,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Arsenical keratoses show a spectrum of morphology ranging from acanthosis, papillomatosis, and hyperkeratosis to squamous dysplasia, often with the dysplastic keratinocytes showing vacuolization, multinucleated forms, and atypical mitotic activity {21050621; 12426152; 23370535; 10397578; 29387754}. The squamous dysplasia does not affect the full-thickness epidermis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124186,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124187,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124188,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> squamoproliferative skin lesions with or without squamous dysplasia in the setting of chronic arsenic exposure.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124189,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124190,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 7,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Arsenical keratoses continue to grow with time and may progress to squamous cell carcinoma, with potential for metastatic disease.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-02-25T14:41:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]